# Files graphify should never scan.
#
# The graph is built with `--code-only`, which extracts nothing from JSON, yet
# the incremental scan still stamps these tracked config files in the manifest.
# A stamped file that yields no nodes is re-queued by graphify on *every*
# refresh — "re-queuing N manifest-stamped code file(s) with no nodes" — and
# that cannot clear itself, because the extraction succeeds rather than failing,
# so the unstamping escape hatch never fires. Each refresh therefore re-parses
# these files and reports a failed extraction that never happened.
#
# `.graphifyignore` is the only rule that works here: graphify exempts
# git-tracked paths from `.gitignore` pruning, so `.gitignore` cannot drop them.
# Nothing is lost from the graph — `--code-only` produced no nodes for any of
# these to begin with.
.vscode/
config/*.json
pyrightconfig.json
